WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:06.030
The interstellar multi-generational colony ship
which once carried the people of Serenity...

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:10.310
Though lacking an FTL drive,
it boasted a cyclical regeneration system

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:16.030
that kept most of its passengers in cold sleep
during its search for a habitable planet.

00:00:16.310 --> 00:00:19.290
This colony ship is the golden ghost ship's true identity.

00:00:19.800 --> 00:00:22.040
Who will find it first:

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.310
Kato Marika's Bentenmaru

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:26.880
or the mysterious Serenity fleet?

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.500
And what is the golden ghost ship's secret?

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:33.010
Let's go, everyone!

00:02:08.430 --> 00:02:09.560
Slight clearing two minutes off the bow.

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.730
Elevation two degrees, one minute.

00:02:11.730 --> 00:02:12.690
Roger.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:15.360
Our output's dropping some, but we can do it!

00:02:15.360 --> 00:02:16.860
With pleasure.

00:02:21.030 --> 00:02:23.530
There may be fighting aboard the ghost ship.

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.820
This time, it's for real.

00:02:26.820 --> 00:02:28.500
Be sure you're prepared to see combat.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.960
Right!

00:02:30.410 --> 00:02:32.910
One Maracot-class battleship,

00:02:32.910 --> 00:02:35.710
with six Corback-class escorts.

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.630
The Queen Serendipity,

00:02:38.630 --> 00:02:40.930
flagship of the Serenity Defense Forces.

00:02:42.550 --> 00:02:44.180
I don't know how much of this is a bluff

00:02:44.180 --> 00:02:46.930
and how much is real equipment.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:52.390
But it has a command transmitter
able to broadcast to the entire fleet.

00:02:52.390 --> 00:02:55.230
It's a strategic battleship
meant for interstellar war.

00:02:55.230 --> 00:03:00.980
Um, do the Serenity Defense Forces
have that many ships to spare?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:03.400
They've even sent their flagship all the way out here.

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.280
Dunno.

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.120
With such a big fleet elsewhere,
I'd worry about my own borders.

00:03:12.450 --> 00:03:13.660
I see.

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:15.630
So they really are serious?

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:18.290
Winning this will be difficult...

00:03:18.290 --> 00:03:18.920
Marika?

00:03:19.670 --> 00:03:23.300
But we don't need to win in an actual fight, right?

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:23.930
Misa!

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:29.480
Would you show Gruier how to put on a spacesuit?

00:03:30.600 --> 00:03:31.440
Sure.

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:34.400
A kid's spacesuit, huh?

00:03:35.270 --> 00:03:36.610
Oh, there's that one...

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.440
Let's go.

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:39.650
Um...

00:03:40.940 --> 00:03:46.530
We may not be able to dock directly,
so there's no harm in learning.

00:03:47.410 --> 00:03:49.540
You're going to fulfill your responsibilities, right?

00:03:51.200 --> 00:03:52.290
Understood.

00:04:06.380 --> 00:04:10.260
So, where do we start, Captain?

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:11.850
What's that fleet been up to?

00:04:11.850 --> 00:04:21.150
They've split their escorts into
a triangular prism around a single location.

00:04:21.150 --> 00:04:27.120
Meaning that they have a good idea of
the next space-time quake's location.

00:04:27.820 --> 00:04:29.780
Any indication that they're concerned with us?

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:31.370
Nothing obvious.

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:34.290
What do you think?

00:04:34.290 --> 00:04:36.130
What will the fleet do now?

00:04:37.370 --> 00:04:44.800
If each escort uses its FTL drive
on the source of that space-time quake,

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:49.180
the odds are favorable that they can
drag the golden ghost ship here.

00:04:50.260 --> 00:04:52.260
So it's time, is it?

00:04:52.260 --> 00:04:59.020
Which means the Bentenmaru's gotta head
straight into the midst of the waiting fleet.

00:05:00.140 --> 00:05:01.230
Yup.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:02.610
That's it.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:05.700
What do you think, Captain?

00:05:06.350 --> 00:05:06.860
About?

00:05:07.900 --> 00:05:12.950
Oh, I just wondered what you were planning,
given that you had the princess leave.

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.080
I'm captain of the Bentenmaru.

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.130
I have to make the decisions
that will protect this ship.

00:05:21.340 --> 00:05:24.460
Thus, the ship's safety is my first priority.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:27.710
Even if it's a job from the
Serenity royal family's princess,

00:05:27.710 --> 00:05:30.590
if things get bad, we run.

00:05:30.590 --> 00:05:32.680
We can't do anything if we're dead.

00:05:33.260 --> 00:05:34.430
Still...

00:05:35.180 --> 00:05:41.360
A smart girl like Gruier even seems troubled.

00:05:41.770 --> 00:05:47.110
She must be thinking of something bad.

00:05:49.940 --> 00:05:51.490
Bad, huh?

00:05:52.070 --> 00:05:56.870
I don't know what it is, and the
Bentenmaru's safety is my top priority.

00:05:56.870 --> 00:05:59.170
I want to do what I can for her.

00:05:59.950 --> 00:06:02.670
So there's something I'd like you to do for me.

00:06:04.750 --> 00:06:05.710
What is it?

00:06:05.710 --> 00:06:07.130
A jump?

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.630
Attention crew! This is your captain, Marika.

00:06:10.630 --> 00:06:12.350
Anyway, let's continue.

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:16.510
The Bentenmaru is now prepping for an FTL jump.

00:06:16.510 --> 00:06:19.060
We'll jump once we've compiled the data.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.980
Upon landing, we may be engaged
in a firefight with a battleship.

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:25.320
Everyone, be ready.

00:06:26.560 --> 00:06:30.030
She should take these announcements more seriously.

00:06:30.030 --> 00:06:34.530
Maybe she found a way to catch the ghost ship.

00:06:34.530 --> 00:06:37.530
What does she mean by
"a firefight with a battleship"?

00:06:37.530 --> 00:06:40.250
Should I return to the bridge?

00:06:40.700 --> 00:06:45.170
Now that she's decided on her course, there won't
be anything you can do even if you go back.

00:06:47.450 --> 00:06:48.630
More importantly...

00:06:49.340 --> 00:06:53.010
Your first job is to master wearing a spacesuit.

00:06:53.010 --> 00:06:55.350
Aren't you boarding the ghost ship?

00:06:57.140 --> 00:06:58.520
That's right.

00:07:02.640 --> 00:07:04.020
Bentenmaru, jump!

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:05.900
Output is high and steady.

00:07:06.230 --> 00:07:08.400
Bentenmaru, commencing FTL jump!

00:07:17.910 --> 00:07:19.870
Watch out for heavy turbulence.

00:07:19.870 --> 00:07:22.160
We're heading into a space-time quake.

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:23.410
I'll do what I can.

00:07:23.410 --> 00:07:25.090
We'll be touching down momentarily.

00:07:36.310 --> 00:07:38.930
This is worse than last time!

00:07:38.930 --> 00:07:39.770
What are you doing?!

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:41.640
Stop whining.

00:07:41.640 --> 00:07:43.140
This was all crazy to begin with.

00:07:43.140 --> 00:07:44.730
You can handle a few warning sirens.

00:07:45.520 --> 00:07:48.270
As long as the Bentenmaru's safe, everything's fine.

00:07:48.270 --> 00:07:49.610
Where's the battleship?

00:07:49.940 --> 00:07:52.110
Just where we deduced.
It's on the other side of the quake.

00:07:52.400 --> 00:07:53.530
Have they seen us?

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:54.200
Probably.

00:07:54.610 --> 00:07:58.330
I have two recon pods just based on sensor readings.

00:07:58.780 --> 00:08:01.200
There are probably more too.

00:08:01.200 --> 00:08:02.750
They're in active observation mode.

00:08:03.200 --> 00:08:04.950
Ignore the recon pods.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:05.960
Where's the ghost ship?

00:08:06.540 --> 00:08:09.290
This space-time quake is different from the others.

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:13.800
I'm seeing space-time vibrations and
energy concentrations, but I can't be sure.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.930
I can say one thing though.

00:08:15.720 --> 00:08:16.390
And that is?

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.430
We'd be safer farther away from the quake.

00:08:29.650 --> 00:08:31.440
I'm seeing multiple intense gravity sources.

00:08:32.700 --> 00:08:36.070
No... It's a single ring-shaped one!

00:08:36.400 --> 00:08:37.120
What is it?

00:08:37.990 --> 00:08:39.330
Hell if I know.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.580
What are these numbers?

00:08:43.580 --> 00:08:45.710
Is a neutron star going to jump out at us?

00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:46.950
Hurry!

00:08:46.950 --> 00:08:48.070
I <i>am</i> hurrying!

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:52.880
We won't make it.

00:09:08.180 --> 00:09:09.150
Huh?

00:09:09.150 --> 00:09:10.770
What happened?

00:09:10.770 --> 00:09:13.820
The expanded gravity ring passed by us.

00:09:14.690 --> 00:09:19.360
A gravity source with no accompanying matter
is passing through us at half the speed of light.

00:09:19.360 --> 00:09:21.620
What's going on?

00:09:22.620 --> 00:09:27.080
There's a spatial rip where the gravity ring originated!

00:09:27.500 --> 00:09:28.790
A spatial rip?

00:09:29.410 --> 00:09:30.210
Get us out of here!

00:09:30.830 --> 00:09:35.340
I don't know what's going on,
but that could tear the ship in half!

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:36.880
San-Daime!

00:09:36.880 --> 00:09:38.260
No holding back.

00:09:38.260 --> 00:09:39.550
Remove all our limiters.

00:09:39.880 --> 00:09:41.050
I'm doing it now.

00:09:41.050 --> 00:09:45.430
You can't just flip off every limiter at once, y'know.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.350
Okay, go!

00:09:47.350 --> 00:09:49.440
Bentenmaru, full speed ahead!

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.370
Shock wave incoming!

00:10:05.910 --> 00:10:07.460
A shock wave in space?

00:10:07.460 --> 00:10:09.540
Space is being torn apart.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.500
That'll cause a shock wave.

00:10:11.500 --> 00:10:13.080
It's going to shake the hull pretty bad.

00:10:13.080 --> 00:10:15.210
Prepare ship for impact!

00:10:22.850 --> 00:10:23.930
Okay...

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:25.930
We're a good distance from the epicenter.

00:10:26.390 --> 00:10:29.020
Instead of running, stabilize the ship.

00:10:29.020 --> 00:10:31.520
The auto-stabilizers are running at full power.

00:10:31.520 --> 00:10:35.230
How are we supposed to handle this thing?

00:10:35.230 --> 00:10:37.490
Hang on... A big one's on the way.

00:10:45.660 --> 00:10:46.160
There it is.

00:10:58.430 --> 00:11:00.970
That's the ghost ship?

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:16.230
Length, twenty-four kilometers.

00:11:16.230 --> 00:11:17.940
At its broadest, seven kilometers wide.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:21.110
It's not that large for a natural satellite.

00:11:21.110 --> 00:11:26.950
But for an ancient ship without
an FTL drive, it's enormous.

00:11:27.870 --> 00:11:29.040
That's gotta be it.

00:11:30.080 --> 00:11:32.190
It's the golden ghost ship.

00:11:35.080 --> 00:11:37.380
Wait... The space around it looks bad.

00:11:37.830 --> 00:11:39.500
I'm seeing high energy readings.

00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:41.260
The rift distortion is going to be released.

00:11:41.550 --> 00:11:44.260
Let's minimize our profile toward the ghost ship.

00:11:44.260 --> 00:11:46.470
This shockwave is going to be as big as a supernova!

00:11:49.260 --> 00:11:50.640
We'll take the impact from the bow.

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:53.350
Pray the hull and engines hold!

00:11:58.740 --> 00:11:59.320
Here it comes.

00:12:24.710 --> 00:12:26.220
Damage report...

00:12:26.220 --> 00:12:28.130
can come later.

00:12:28.130 --> 00:12:31.560
For now, get our systems back on-line
so the Bentenmaru can move.

00:12:32.010 --> 00:12:33.470
We're okay.

00:12:33.470 --> 00:12:36.190
I isolated them before the overload.

00:12:36.560 --> 00:12:40.770
So we don't need to reboot the radar or sensors.

00:12:40.770 --> 00:12:41.900
But uh, sorry...

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:44.910
The comms went down!

00:12:45.580 --> 00:12:49.660
I'm gonna have to reconfigure everything...

00:12:50.490 --> 00:12:51.790
Did we lose the combat systems too?

00:12:52.120 --> 00:12:53.910
Reconfiguring now.

00:12:53.910 --> 00:12:56.460
Missiles and the main gun are still operative.

00:12:57.660 --> 00:13:00.710
I have our position, and the space-time quake is gone.

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.390
Set a course for the golden ghost ship!

00:13:14.570 --> 00:13:16.520
So where do we board?

00:13:16.520 --> 00:13:18.480
Gather data while we approach.

00:13:19.140 --> 00:13:23.610
According to the reports,
there should be docking ports on either side.

00:13:24.110 --> 00:13:25.780
The battleship's moving too.

00:13:29.360 --> 00:13:30.400
This course...

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.360
They aren't heading toward the ghost ship.

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:33.750
They're coming directly at us.

00:13:37.540 --> 00:13:39.290
What happened?!

00:13:39.790 --> 00:13:41.120
Sorry.

00:13:41.120 --> 00:13:44.210
Combat systems aren't on-line yet.

00:13:44.210 --> 00:13:47.300
I was getting the ship systems back on-line first.

00:13:47.300 --> 00:13:48.720
It's fine.

00:13:49.050 --> 00:13:52.970
There's your golden ghost ship.

00:14:00.230 --> 00:14:02.770
Bringing comm systems back on-line.

00:14:02.770 --> 00:14:04.320
Starting with normal comms.

00:14:05.270 --> 00:14:06.900
Thought so... Got one.

00:14:06.900 --> 00:14:07.900
From whom?

00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.530
There's only one group

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:13.740
who'd send us an emergency message in this situation.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:20.000
"From: Serenity Defense Forces, Flagship Queen Serendipity.

00:14:20.000 --> 00:14:23.750
Sender: Grunhilde Serenity."

00:14:25.920 --> 00:14:27.630
It has a designated recipient.

00:14:27.630 --> 00:14:32.890
It says "Gruier Serenity, on board the Bentenmaru."

00:14:33.470 --> 00:14:34.930
Grunhilde?

00:14:34.930 --> 00:14:38.100
So they couldn't be bothered to
greet the captain first, huh?

00:14:38.100 --> 00:14:39.940
They have guts.

00:14:41.350 --> 00:14:43.570
Grunhilde Serenity...

00:14:44.140 --> 00:14:46.530
Eighth princess of the Serenity royal family, yes?

00:14:49.400 --> 00:14:50.450
She's my younger sister.

00:14:55.610 --> 00:14:59.960
She came all this way for the ghost ship.

00:15:01.640 --> 00:15:03.000
Gruier, you're up!

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:06.710
You're going to answer the message, aren't you?

00:15:06.710 --> 00:15:10.510
Then you should be sitting in the captain's chair.

00:15:14.130 --> 00:15:15.010
Okay.

00:15:16.430 --> 00:15:20.980
Kane, get us to the ghost ship immediately.

00:15:21.390 --> 00:15:22.730
I'm on it.

00:15:33.240 --> 00:15:34.280
Opening a channel.

00:15:36.320 --> 00:15:38.580
Please leave, Gruier.

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:41.370
Her sister's pretty too.

00:15:41.370 --> 00:15:42.790
What are you looking at?

00:15:43.120 --> 00:15:48.000
You know what we must do, right?

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:49.260
Please leave.

00:15:49.710 --> 00:15:52.840
What is the meaning of that uniform, Grunhilde?

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:58.550
You know what it means for a member of the royal family

00:15:58.550 --> 00:16:01.390
to fly a battleship in uniform, Hilde.

00:16:01.390 --> 00:16:05.390
A ruler must lead from the battle's front line.

00:16:05.390 --> 00:16:07.560
Of course I am aware.

00:16:07.560 --> 00:16:12.110
That is what I'm doing aboard the Queen Serendipity.

00:16:12.690 --> 00:16:16.370
Grunhilde, you're being manipulated, right?

00:16:17.530 --> 00:16:21.530
I'm on this ship of my own free will.

00:16:21.530 --> 00:16:24.880
I don't want to hear a word from someone who's
lowered themselves to the level of a pirate!

00:16:25.290 --> 00:16:30.760
I will not allow you to insult this ship or its crew!

00:16:35.210 --> 00:16:38.600
Please just leave, Gruier.

00:16:39.180 --> 00:16:42.930
If you don't, I'll have no choice but to use force.

00:16:42.930 --> 00:16:44.560
Stop your ship.

00:16:44.560 --> 00:16:47.180
The Queen Serendipity's gunports are already

00:16:47.180 --> 00:16:50.070
open and targeting your pirate ship.

00:16:56.570 --> 00:16:59.910
Grunhilde, I'm going on ahead.

00:16:59.910 --> 00:17:02.830
If you wish to stop me,
let's meet inside the ghost ship.

00:17:04.910 --> 00:17:06.290
Gruier...

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:08.340
High energy readings!

00:17:12.980 --> 00:17:14.170
An attack?

00:17:14.170 --> 00:17:15.420
No.

00:17:15.420 --> 00:17:19.010
An omni-directional, high-output
radar scan from the ghost ship!

00:17:20.380 --> 00:17:22.640
I thought it was dead.

00:17:22.640 --> 00:17:24.310
It woke up.

00:17:56.740 --> 00:17:58.090
A message we can't refuse!

00:18:00.350 --> 00:18:01.590
Wow...

00:18:01.590 --> 00:18:04.720
Uncompressed double-digital communications.

00:18:04.720 --> 00:18:06.240
Old-school!

00:18:06.240 --> 00:18:07.850
Can you read it?

00:18:07.850 --> 00:18:08.850
Don't worry.

00:18:08.850 --> 00:18:10.480
It's fundamentally a simple code.

00:18:10.930 --> 00:18:14.030
If we use it properly, we can communicate with it.

00:18:17.860 --> 00:18:21.150
The first two lines are the ship's name and registration.

00:18:21.150 --> 00:18:25.070
This is Serenity Interstellar Trading's first ship.

00:18:25.070 --> 00:18:28.000
It is named Queen Serendipity.

00:18:32.460 --> 00:18:36.800
It's a traditional name for Serenity ships.

00:18:37.290 --> 00:18:39.510
The rest is an ID code.

00:18:39.510 --> 00:18:43.390
Our response will determine if it
recognizes us as a friend or foe.

00:18:44.010 --> 00:18:46.520
Princess, can you handle this?

00:18:47.600 --> 00:18:49.810
Yes, of course.

00:18:57.480 --> 00:19:00.980
I'm seeing six pre-drives around us.

00:19:00.980 --> 00:19:02.570
Hurry, Kane!

00:19:02.570 --> 00:19:05.080
We need to dock with the ghost ship
before the escorts arrive.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:07.040
It'll be close, but I'll get it done.

00:19:07.570 --> 00:19:09.330
Withdrawing all antenna masts!

00:19:09.330 --> 00:19:10.420
We're going in backwards!

00:19:18.030 --> 00:19:19.500
Wait, Kane.

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:20.970
This isn't normal docking speed!

00:19:21.880 --> 00:19:23.220
We're in combat.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:34.480
Kane!

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:36.440
Final deceleration.

00:19:49.070 --> 00:19:50.870
We got smacked in the butt!

00:19:51.200 --> 00:19:52.580
We're fine.

00:19:52.580 --> 00:19:55.330
It didn't hurt the hull structure.

00:19:55.330 --> 00:19:57.380
San-Daime, how do the nozzles look?

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:01.670
Not seeing any major damage...

00:20:01.670 --> 00:20:04.850
But I'm sure you scratched the stern up pretty bad.

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:07.810
The hatch is closing.

00:20:11.600 --> 00:20:14.430
The Bentenmaru is locked in.

00:20:14.430 --> 00:20:17.060
I can see that much...

00:20:17.060 --> 00:20:19.270
So, Princess...

00:20:19.270 --> 00:20:23.150
We caught your ghost ship,
or maybe it caught us, but...

00:20:23.150 --> 00:20:25.700
We're here.

00:20:26.320 --> 00:20:28.490
Thank you.

00:20:39.080 --> 00:20:41.010
I can handle the rest.

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:46.300
I must attend to something within the ghost ship.

00:20:46.300 --> 00:20:49.680
Could you wait somewhere safe?

00:20:50.010 --> 00:20:51.640
Then we'll wait here!

00:20:52.600 --> 00:20:53.720
No...

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:55.600
I'm happy, but...

00:20:56.060 --> 00:20:58.520
There's a fleet outside.

00:20:58.520 --> 00:21:01.550
The safest place is inside the ghost ship.

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:02.780
But...

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:04.980
What was that?

00:21:04.980 --> 00:21:05.820
We're shaking.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.990
It's a space-time quake!

00:21:07.990 --> 00:21:09.150
This is...

00:21:09.150 --> 00:21:11.370
We're going back into subspace?

00:21:11.700 --> 00:21:13.000
Subspace?

00:21:18.710 --> 00:21:20.080
Lock down the ship!

00:21:20.080 --> 00:21:21.050
Prepare for jump!

00:21:21.460 --> 00:21:22.800
Launching anchor.

00:21:28.420 --> 00:21:30.140
Listen, Gruier.

00:21:30.800 --> 00:21:35.640
When the ghost ship finishes
its jump, I'm coming with you.

00:21:37.270 --> 00:21:42.280
If I told you that I'm going alone,
you wouldn't listen, would you?

00:21:46.530 --> 00:21:51.200
It's the captain's job to protect
the crew and passengers.

00:21:52.450 --> 00:21:55.120
I can't send you out there alone.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:21:59.500
The ghost ship is jumping.

00:22:01.750 --> 00:22:04.970
All crew, brace for impact!

00:22:06.090 --> 00:22:08.260
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.390
Wanderer of Light
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:11.390 --> 00:22:12.470
C.M.S. C.M.A. O.P.R. Into the space

00:22:12.470 --> 00:22:17.980
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:17.980 --> 00:22:20.980
Welcome glory, let's breakthrough and fly out now, let's go!

00:22:20.980 --> 00:22:24.360
Run towards an unlimited dimension. Come, let's accelerate beyond this

00:22:24.360 --> 00:22:27.450
history that's to be known, regardless of time. Fly towards a destined future.

00:22:27.450 --> 00:22:30.490
Just a fossil if you give up a miracle. Your decision is your best choice.

00:22:32.080 --> 00:22:39.420
There's another, unknown, me hiding in my heart.

00:22:39.420 --> 00:22:44.300
M.C.Z. Overall O.I.E. What's goin' on?

00:22:44.590 --> 00:22:48.130
How far?

00:22:48.130 --> 00:22:50.800
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell! Go, go, ring, ring a bell!

00:22:50.800 --> 00:22:54.430
Until the end.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.770
Go, go, go, go, ring a bell!

00:22:55.770 --> 00:22:59.100
You're lost and missing.

00:23:00.480 --> 00:23:07.940
We're lost without a hope of any shelter.

00:23:07.940 --> 00:23:11.700
But why? What did we do? What did we do?

00:23:11.700 --> 00:23:13.120
What should we do?

00:23:13.120 --> 00:23:16.290
From the world beyond shadows invade.

00:23:16.290 --> 00:23:20.580
We're destined to stop them with our lives.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:26.630
So no matter where we go, as far as it takes

00:23:26.630 --> 00:23:30.880
we'll always believe in ourselves.

00:23:38.760 --> 00:23:40.960
The ghost ship reveals its full size,

00:23:40.960 --> 00:23:43.440
and regains its golden glow.

00:23:43.810 --> 00:23:46.110
The royal family's dream...
Political strife...

00:23:46.860 --> 00:23:49.570
The two princesses have become enemies.
Will they ever reconcile?

00:23:50.740 --> 00:23:53.740
And what brilliant strategy
will Captain Marika employ?

00:23:54.530 --> 00:23:56.330
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:56.330 --> 00:23:57.330
A return from eternity.

00:23:57.330 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
A Return from Eternity

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.460
We'll take the impact
from the bow.
